# ─── VENDOR FIRMWARE: COMMITTED, NOT IGNORED (docs/wifi.md 8) ─────────────────
#
# This block used to ignore `*.bin` firmware patterns, on the reasoning that Linux keeps no blobs in its
# kernel tree. THAT DECISION WAS REVERSED THE SAME DAY, and the patterns are gone rather than left to
# forbid what the policy now requires - a guard that contradicts its own rule is worse than none, because
# the next person trusts it.
#
# What changed: Linux's separation is Debian's social contract and the DFSG, not a technical conclusion,
# and a fetch-at-setup script has to reimplement someone else's packaging logic. Proven the hard way in
# one sitting - the board-specific name is a symlink, into a SIBLING directory, to a filename that does
# not exist in the tree because the packaging rules create it at build time. Every one of those failures
# would have been a user's failure with a silent radio.
#
# So redistributable device firmware IS committed, under `nonfree/<part>/`, with its LICENCE beside it and
# a PROVENANCE record carrying the upstream URL and a SHA-256 per file. `scripts/nonfree_check.py` enforces
# both on every build, so the policy is mechanical rather than remembered. Firmware whose licence does NOT
# permit redistribution stays out and is fetched on the owner's machine by `scripts/get_firmware.py`.
